\begin{vmatrix}
9 & -18 & -16 & 0 \\
0 & 9 & -18 & -16 \\
15 & 28 & 12 & 0 \\
0 & 15 & 28 & 12
\end{vmatrix}
\] By expanding the determinant, we get the resultant as \(228x^2 + 432x + 144 = 0\). Dividing the entire equation by the greatest common divisor of the coefficients (24), we get \(7x^2 + 18x + 6 = 0\). Solving this quadratic equation using the quadratic formula \(x = \frac{-b \pm \sqrt{b^2 - 4ac}}{2a}\), where \(a = 7\), \(b = 18\), and \(c = 6\), we get: \[
