\] Since both solutions must satisfy both original equations, we check which of these solutions is valid. By substituting \(x = \frac{-9 + \sqrt{39}}{7}\) into both equations, we can verify that it satisfies both. Therefore, the value of \(x\) is \(\frac{-9 + \sqrt{39}}{7}\). \</think> <answer> \(\frac{-9 + \sqrt{39}}{7}\) </answer>

